   "source": [
    "# Road Scene Understanding & Multi-Class Object Recognition using YOLOv8\n",
    "**College PBL project: runs on a CPU laptop (no GPU needed)**\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why YOLO?\n",
    "**YOLO (\"You Only Look Once\")** is a CNN that looks at the whole image once and predicts all bounding boxes and classes together. That makes it fast enough for real-time driving use, unlike two-stage detectors such as Faster R-CNN.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What this notebook does\n",
    "| Step | Task |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| 1 | Detect road objects (car, bus, truck, person, bicycle, motorcycle, traffic light, stop sign) with a pretrained **YOLOv8n** |\n",
    "| 2 | **Scene understanding:** where is each object (left / ahead / right, near / far) and is there a hazard? |\n",
    "| 3 | Run on **video**, count objects over time and count unique objects with tracking |\n",
    "| 4 | **Evaluate** the model (precision, recall, mAP) |\n",
    "| 5 | *(Optional)* **Fine-tune** on the KITTI driving dataset |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "46db74fe",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Run once if needed (then restart the kernel):\n",
    "# %pip install ultralytics opencv-python matplotlib"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "67bdecc5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup and load YOLOv8"
   ]
  },
   {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "064c4b3b",
   "metadata": {},
    "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os, time, urllib.request\n",
    "import cv2\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from ultralytics import YOLO\n",
    "\n",
    "MODEL_NAME = \"yolov8n.pt\"    # 'n' = nano (fastest on CPU). Try yolov8s.pt for better accuracy.\n",
    "CONF   = 0.35               # confidence threshold\n",
    "IMGSZ  = 640                # inference size (use 416 for faster CPU speed)\n",
    "\n",
    "model = YOLO(MODEL_NAME)    # weights download automatically the first time\n",
    "print(\"Classes the model knows:\", len(model.names))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Road-relevant classes (COCO names + KITTI names, so the same code works after fine-tuning)\n",
    "ROAD_CLASSES = {\"person\", \"bicycle\", \"car\", \"motorcycle\", \"bus\", \"truck\", \"traffic light\", \"stop sign\",\n",
    "                \"van\", \"pedestrian\", \"cyclist\", \"tram\"}\n",
    "VULNERABLE   = {\"person\", \"bicycle\", \"motorcycle\", \"pedestrian\", \"cyclist\"}\n",
    "VEHICLES     = {\"car\", \"bus\", \"truck\", \"van\", \"tram\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "def road_ids(m):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Class ids of the road-related classes for a given model.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return [i for i, n in m.names.items() if n in ROAD_CLASSES]\n",
    "print(\"Road class ids:\", {i: model.names[i] for i in road_ids(model)})"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "961e426d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Detect objects in a road image\n",
    "Put your own street photo in the notebook folder and set `IMAGE_PATH`. If the file does not exist, a sample street image is downloaded."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "671c92db",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "IMAGE_PATH = \"street.jpg\"   # <- change to your own road photo\n",
    "SAMPLE_URL = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/main/ultralytics/assets/bus.jpg\"\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(IMAGE_PATH):\n",
    "    urllib.request.urlretrieve(SAMPLE_URL, IMAGE_PATH)\n",
    "    print(\"Downloaded sample image ->\", IMAGE_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "def detect(src, conf=CONF, m=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Run YOLO and return (raw result, list of road-object detections).\"\"\"\n",
    "    m = m or model\n",
    "    r = m(src, conf=conf, imgsz=IMGSZ, classes=road_ids(m), verbose=False)[0]\n",
    "    dets = [{\"name\": r.names[int(b.cls)], \"conf\": float(b.conf), \"box\": b.xyxy[0].tolist()}\n",
    "            for b in r.boxes]\n",
    "    return r, dets\n",
    "\n",
    "t0 = time.time()\n",
    "result, dets = detect(IMAGE_PATH)\n",
    "print(f\"Inference took {time.time()-t0:.2f}s - found {len(dets)} road objects\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 8))\n",
    "plt.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(result.plot(), cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)); plt.axis(\"off\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"YOLOv8 detections\"); plt.show()\n",
    "for d in dets:\n",
    "    print(f\"{d['name']:14s} conf={d['conf']:.2f}  box={[round(v) for v in d['box']]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0a591a0f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Scene understanding\n",
    "Detection alone says *what* is there. A driving system also needs *where* and *how risky*. We add simple geometric rules:\n",
    "- **Zone:** left / ahead / right, from the box centre (horizontal thirds of the image).\n",
    "- **Near / far:** an object is *near* if its bottom edge is low in the image or its box is tall (closer to the camera).\n",
    "- **Hazard rules:** a vulnerable road user (pedestrian, cyclist, motorcyclist) **ahead and near** gives a BRAKE warning, a vehicle ahead and near gives KEEP DISTANCE, and so on."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8aebfce5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def analyze_scene(dets, shape):\n",
    "    H, W = shape[:2]\n",
    "    rows, warnings = [], []\n",
    "    for d in dets:\n",
    "        x1, y1, x2, y2 = d[\"box\"]\n",
    "        cx = (x1 + x2) / 2 / W\n",
    "        zone = \"left\" if cx < 1/3 else (\"ahead\" if cx < 2/3 else \"right\")\n",
    "        near = (y2 / H > 0.75) or ((y2 - y1) / H > 0.35)\n",
    "        rows.append((d[\"name\"], zone, \"near\" if near else \"far\", d[\"conf\"]))\n",
    "        if d[\"name\"] in VULNERABLE and zone == \"ahead\" and near:\n",
    "            warnings.append(f\"BRAKE: {d['name']} close ahead\")\n",
    "        elif d[\"name\"] in VULNERABLE and zone == \"ahead\":\n",
    "            warnings.append(f\"CAUTION: {d['name']} ahead\")\n",
    "        elif d[\"name\"] in VEHICLES and zone == \"ahead\" and near:\n",
    "            warnings.append(f\"KEEP DISTANCE: {d['name']} close ahead\")\n",
    "        elif d[\"name\"] == \"stop sign\":\n",
    "            warnings.append(\"INFO: stop sign detected\")\n",
    "        elif d[\"name\"] == \"traffic light\":\n",
    "            warnings.append(\"INFO: traffic light detected")\n",
    "     counts = {}\n",
    "    for n, *_ in rows:\n",
    "        counts[n] = counts.get(n, 0) + 1\n",
    "    summary = (\"Scene: \" + \", \".join(f\"{v} {k}\" for k, v in counts.items())) if counts else \"No road objects detected.\"\n",
    "    return rows, sorted(set(warnings)), summary\n",
    "\n",
    "img = cv2.imread(IMAGE_PATH)\n",
    "rows, warnings, summary = analyze_scene(dets, img.shape)\n",
    "print(summary, \"\\n\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'object':14s}{'zone':8s}{'distance':9s}conf\")\n",
    "for n, z, d_, c in rows:\n",
    "    print(f\"{n:14s}{z:8s}{d_:9s}{c:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nAlerts:\", warnings or \"none\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8cdff0e5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize the zones: dashed lines split the image\n",
    "\n",
    "img_zoned = image.copy()\n",
    "h1, w1 = img_zoned.shape[:2]\n",
    "for x in (w1 / 3, 2 * w1 / 3):\n",
    "    x = int(x)\n",
    "    cv2.line(img_zoned, x z, 0), x1, h1), (255, 255, 0), 2)\n",
    "thres = int(.0.75 * h1)\n",
    "cv2.line(img_zoned, (0, thres), (w1, thres), (0, 165, 255), 2)\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "plt.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(img_zoned, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)); plt.axis(\"off\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Scene zones and near line\"); plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4. Video inference\n",
    "    open the video as with CV2 and proces every stride frame. The full repository utility is in project: scripts/run_video.py.\"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "221d1a27",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Count UNIQUE objects with tracking (each object keeps one ID, so a car is not counted 100 times)\n",
    "def count_unique(path, conf=CONF, max_frames=MAX_FRAMES):\n",
    "    seen = {}\n",
    "    stream = model.track(source=path, conf=conf, imgsz=IMGSZ, classes=road_ids(model),\n",
    "                         persist=True, stream=True, verbose=False)\n",
    "    for k, r in enumerate(stream):\n",
    "        if r.boxes.id is not None:\n",
    "            for tid, c in zip(r.boxes.id.int().tolist(), r.boxes.cls.int().tolist()):\n",
    "                seen.setdefault(r.names[c], set()).add(tid)\n",
    "        if k >= max_frames:\n",
    "            break\n",
    "    return {n: len(s) for n, s in seen.items()}\n",
    "\n",
    "if os.path.exists(VIDEO_PATH):\n",
    "     try:\n",
    "        print(\"Unique objects in the clip:\", count_unique(VIDEO_PATH))\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        print(\"Tracking skipped:\", e)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f39f561b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Evaluation\n",
    "Standard object-detection metrics:\n",
    "- **Precision**: of the boxes predicted, how many are right?\n",
    "- **Recall**: of the real objects, how many were found?\n",
    "- **mAP50**: average precision at IoU 0.5; **mAP50-95**: average over stricter IoU thresholds (the main metric).\n",
    "\n",
    "Here we validate on **COCO8** (a tiny 8-image sample that downloads automatically) just to demonstrate the pipeline. For a real number, use KITTI or COCO val in Section 6."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "abcce4d7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "val = model.val(data=\"coco8.yaml\", imgsz=IMGSZ, device=\"cpu\", plots=False, verbose=False)\n",
    "print(f\"Precision {val.box.mp:.3f} | Recall {val.box.mr:.3f} | mAP50 {val.box.map50:.3f} | mAP50-95 {val.box.map:.3f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nPer-class mAP50-95 (classes present in this tiny set):\")\n",
    "for c, ap in zip(val.box.ap_class_index, val.box.maps[val.box.ap_class_index]):\n",
    "    mark = \"  <- road class\" if val.names[int(c)] in ROAD_CLASSES else \"\"\n",
    "    print(f\"  {val.names[int(c)]:14s} {ap:.3f}{mark}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0f56b8fa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. (Optional) Fine-tune on a driving dataset (KITTI)",
    "Pretrained COCO weights are general. Fine-tuning on **KITTI** (real driving images with car, van, truck, pedestrian, cyclist, tram) adapts YOLO to road scenes. On a CPU, keep it small: a fraction of the data, small image size and few epochs, so expect roughly **15-40 minutes**. A free Google Colab GPU makes it a few minutes.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Set `RUN_FINETUNE = True` to run. KITTI downloads automatically (about 390 MB).\n",
    "- For a back-to-back pipeline demo, use coco8.yaml."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "944adf1e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "RUN_FINETUNE = False\n",
    "FT_DATA   = \"kitti.yaml\"     # or \"coco8.yaml\" for a quick demo\n",
    "FT_EPOCHS = 3\n",
    "FT_FRACTION = 0.1            # use 10% of the training images (CPU-friendly)\n",
    "\n",
    "if RUN_FINETUNE:\n",
    "    ft_model = YOLO(MODEL_NAME)\n",
    "    ft_model.train(data=FT_DATA, epochs=FT_EPOCHS, imgsz=416, batch=8, fraction=FT_FRACTION,\n",
    "                   device=\"cpu\", workers=2, plots=True, project=\"runs\", name=\"road_ft\", exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    best = YOLO(\"runs/detect/runs/road_ft/weights/best.pt\")   # check the path printed by training\n",
    "    m_ft = best.val(data=FT_DATA, imgsz=416, device=\"cpu\", plots=False, verbose=False)\n",
    "    print(f\"FINE-TUNED -> Precision {m_ft.box.mp:.3f} | Recall {m_ft.box.mr:.3f} | \"\n",
    "          f\"mAP50 {m_ft.box.map50:.3f} | mAP50-95 {m_ft.box.map:.3f}\")\n",
    "    # use the fine-tuned model for scene analysis\n",
    "    r_ft, dets_ft = detect(IMAGE_PATH, m=best)\n",
    "    print(analyze_scene(dets_ft, img.shape)[2])\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Fine-tuning skipped (set RUN_FINETUNE = True to run it).\")"
   ]
  },
