    "## 7. Results & discussion\n",
    "*(Fill in with your own numbers after running.)*\n",
    "\n",
    "| Item | Result |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Model | YOLOv8n (3.2 M parameters) |\n",
    "| CPU inference time per image | ___ s |\n",
    "| Precision / Recall | ___ / ___ |\n",
    "| mAP50 / mAP50-95 | ___ / ___ |\n",
    "| Fine-tuned mAP50-95 on KITTI (if run) | ___ |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Observations to discuss**\n",
    "- YOLOv8n is fast on CPU, but small objects (distant cars, traffic lights) are missed more often.\n",
    "- Lower `CONF` finds more objects but gives more false alarms. Try 0.2 / 0.35 / 0.5.\n",
    "- A larger input size (`IMGSZ`) or model (`yolov8s.pt`) improves accuracy but slows inference.\n",
    "- Night, rain and occlusion reduce accuracy.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Limitations:** the distance and zone rules use image geometry only, not real depth. COCO has no specific traffic-sign classes except \"stop sign\".\n",
    "\n",
    "**Future work:** train on a traffic-sign dataset (e.g. GTSRB-detection) so YOLO reads every sign, add lane detection, add monocular depth estimation, export to ONNX and run on a Raspberry Pi or Jetson, and add real-time webcam inference.\n",
    "\n",
    "## References\n",
    "- Redmon et al., *You Only Look Once: Unified, Real-Time Object Detection*, CVPR 2016.\n",
    "- Jocher et al., *Ultralytics YOLOv8*, https://docs.ultralytics.com\n",
    "- Geiger et al., *Are we ready for Autonomous Driving? The KITTI Vision Benchmark Suite*, CVPR 2012.\n",
    "- Lin et al., *Microsoft COCO: Common Objects in Context*, ECCV 2014."
   ]
